        <p>Corporation of Wariington— Public Lighting Water Account l5 16 7 Hospital Account --- 0914 5 Manchester Port Sanitary Authority ...... 22 410 Other Payments, viz., Analysis, Zcc Balance carried forward</p>
        <p>Most gratifying is it to your Board that they aro able to report a greater Increase in Funds than on any previous occasion ; the said increase being £48,978; such a record as this the Board are perhaps pardonably proud to announce. The Investments of the Society are all of a satisfactory character, and their Interest earning capacity is still increasing; the rate they are now earning being equal tea percentage of 3.78 of the Totat _Funds, as against 3.67, wnich it is submitted, ought to give great satisfaction. In conclusion, your Board of Management take this opportunity of acknowledging their most cordial thanks to the Inside and Outsid3 Stalls for the most hearty and willing support they have rendered throughout the very strenuous year, by which alone they are able to report so favourably to the Members. PtICLID. PEEL.</p>
        <p>Secretary.</p>
        <p>'UNDS AND EFFECTS.</p>
        <p>ASSETS.</p>
        <p>£ s. d.</p>
        <p>By Cash Mortgaged on Prope7t-y- situate in England „ Mortgagedion Rates of Corporations Urban and Rural Councils, etc , in various parts of Great Britain 317,817 18 3 „ Invested in/on Offices, Chief and District „ In handsof District Superintendents and Agents to meet Claims „ In Manchester and Liverpool District Bank 10,921 2 1 „ In Secretary's and Treasurer's hands 751 19 11 „ Deposits • Advanced to and return- able by Approved Society for Prelim- inary Expenses 2., Expended for and return- able by Approved Society for General Expenses</p>
        <p>1,020 0 0</p>
        <p>1,613 6 8</p>
        <p>£652,976 2 0</p>
        <p>AUDITORS' CERTIFICATE. 3, KING STREET, BINACBURN, FEBRUARY lanr, 1913. To, TIIE MEMBERS OF TIER BLACKBURN PHILANTHROPIC FRIENDLY COLLECTING SOCIETY.</p>
        <p>Ladies and Gantlemen,—We have examined the Accounts of the society for the year ending December 31st, 1912, and hereby certify them to be correct, duly vouched, and in accordance with law. In the presence of the President, Secretary, and Trustees of the Society, we have inspected the Mortgage Deeds and other Securities belonging to the Society, and have found them in order. We have also ascertained that the Balance in the Bank is correct. We are, yours faithfully, WM. PORTER, )Chartered Accountants e RICHARD R. PORTER. f Auditors. DISTRICT OFFICE: CARLTON HOUSE CHAMBERS, SA.NKEV STREET, WARRING-TON, AND 42, WARGRAVE ROAD, EARLESTOWN. SVPEBINTENDENT : JOSEPH FAIRHURST.</p>
        <p>1'</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-04-12_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
