        <p>A case which slicrs the immeasurable superiority of Dr. Cassell's Tablets over all ordinary drug- medicines and patent foods is that of little Archie Peels, the month old baby of Mrs Louisa Peers, of 14, May-lane, King's Heath, Birmingham. Mrs. Peers says : -" My little boy began to ail when Id and just waited away because be could keep nothing on his stomach. Doctor's medicine did him no gocd, neither did the patent foods ordered, and baby went on getting weaker and weaker and thinner till he was ;ke a little mummy. His gs and arms were drawn tight'y against his body, lis I:tile backbone and ' ones canie through the I mean that the</p>
        <p>, skin was really broken and raw and had to be dressed. We took him to hospital, but were no more successful. Then we heard of Dr. Cassell's Tablets and tried them, and I would not have believed anything could have acted Fo beneficially nor so quiAly. In a tnontli he was so imprived that fi iends wou!d hArdly believe he was the same baby." Dr. Cas,•ell's Tablets act more brilliantly than any other medicine known in cases of Nervous Breakdown, Aruernia, Dability, Sleeplessness, Nerve Pains, Heart Wealine,s, Kidney and Stomlch Disorders, Children's Weakness, Spinal and Nerve Paralysis, and general bodily fatigue, brain fag, and all run-down conditions Sand 2d. to-day to Dr. Cassell's Co., Ltd, 418, Chester- road, Manchester, for a free sample. All Chemists sell Dr. Cassell's Tablets at 101 d., is. lfl. and 2s. 9d.</p>
