        <head>RUNCORN AND WIDNES</head>
        <p>RUNCORN AND WIDNES</p>
        <p>1.1 ALLEGED EMBEZZLEMENT. At \\::',IINIISVS' MANAGER FOR TRIAL. tkitat'agerL:B' ne Tuf-sday, Stewart Dunn, a dentists,' charged that while in the service of Berns of nBB' Irkers de ti t of Blackpool, he embezzled ' s, .£4 and £3 lo -s and falsified the account, L It a 7 m estated by Superintendent Foster that prisones 4,eslisg9ruwa,rY, was asked to make a statement as to hir 'Jane it', Patients from whom he had collected disr,,,b! and which he had not accounted for.Prisober was :Ikltitedt. en February 28th, and left tho district on • arrested-it' A warrant was obtainei and Dunn was*clhe7-i 41 Cheadle Staffordshire. When charged with the tr",.,``'nlent he replied. "I did not fraudulently steal and in replY to the charge of falsification The d'a net do it with intent to defraud." a Prisoner was committed to take his trial at the —rP°°l Quarter Sessions. rOOLT HEALTH OF WIDNES. In PRACTICE IN 111EASLES CASES. C s ii'S annual report as medical ( Meer of IVidnes Dr heel), rehner reports that the town, which has hitherto 01t5l,F.'ttn„0ti,gst those with the highest infantile ;ecord.- ~-J, last year experienced the lowest rate on 4,30 for tilhe figures were 117 per 1,000 births, as against `4e Whole of England and Wales. In 1011 the Of a Orate was 168. Dr Brehner urges the provision turthele.alth visitor, which would do much towards Ref. I..edecitie the rate. sto the experience of a severe epidemic. of 41ds'"' )ta,using the de '25. ,ith of children, the cotor -,cst• "snY people still have the idea that children O (Utet, Lract measles at some time or other, and one tljfildr,7,ears of the foolish practice whereby all the are shut up in one room to get it over together. • ',c_?uld be more disastreus, as most. of the deaths rEvent:'"2er five years of age. If children could be f..iror!,a' getting the disease until after they Iher lave the danger is greatly lessened.' ;essit r,-;"nx. of se me 500 workmen into the town as the the erection of a new works, leads the docto