        <p>RUGBY FOOTBALL. THE NORTHERN UNION. Results of Saturday's Matches. NORTHERN RUGBY LEAGUE. G. T. P. G. T. P. Leeds 3 6 24 Wakefield Trin... 0 1 3 Hunslet 5 7 31 Coventry St Helens 1 6 20 Leigh 0 0 0 Bradford Northn 1 6 20 Halifax Batley Salford Wigan Hull Rochdale Hornets 2 2 10 Widnes Hull Kingston R 1 2 8 Keighley Oldban.l 1 1 5 Barrow NORTHERN RUGBY COMBINATION. Leeds A 1 311 Wakefield T A... 0 1 3 Dewsbury A — 25 Hull A Leigh A Wigan A MANCHESTER AND DISTRICT LEAGUE. RYLANDS' RECREATION V PENDLETON. Bylands scored a decisive win in their return match which was played on the Gorsey-lane enclosure on Saturday. A high wind prevailed, so that some allow- ance was made for any erratic passing. It was some time before the home lot got their passing machinery going, but directly Stretford had beaten Royle, the Pendleton custodian, all was plain sailing. Horrooks put on the finishing touch to an accurate movement towards the right. and Floyd landed the extra points.</p>
        <p>Carter also scored. It was in the second half that the Recreation asserted themselves in decisive fashion, and tries were scord by Horrocks, Slater, Warren, Leah and CArter, goals being placed by Morris and Warren. Result: Rylands' Recreation, 30 points; Pendleton, nil. TO-DAY'S TEAM. RYLANDS RECS. V FLIXTON.—At Flixton. Full back, A Bramhall : three-quarter backs, J Griffiths, W Leab, S Carter, A Horrocks ; half-backs, G Warren, J Calk!): forwards, A Stretford, J Brandwood, H Morris, F Mason, A Booth, B Slater. Reserves, G Floyd and J Broadhurst.</p>
